{
	"description": "Golden vectors for the parameters of send_text (kind text), send_key (kind key) and send_shortcut (kind shortcut): what a stored value types or presses. Replayed by the macOS, Linux and Windows suites against the vocabulary _shared/modules/actions/send_keys.json. A vector with `repeat` stands for its value repeated that many times.",
	"rule": {
		"text": "Valid when it holds between 1 and text_max_code_points code points and no control character (U+0000 to U+001F, U+007F to U+009F). It is typed exactly as stored: nothing is trimmed.",
		"key": "The value is trimmed of ASCII whitespace. It names a key when, with A to Z lowered, it equals the id or an alias of a send_keys.json key; the canonical form is that id. Otherwise it is valid when it is exactly one code point that is not a control character, which is pressed as that character, case kept. Anything else, including an empty value, is invalid.",
		"shortcut": "The value is trimmed of ASCII whitespace. When it ends with ++ the key is + and the modifiers are what precedes the last two characters; otherwise it is split on +, the last part is the key and the others are modifiers. Each modifier, trimmed and with A to Z lowered, must be the id or an alias of a send_keys.json modifier, at least one is required, and two may not name the same id. The key follows the key rule, except that a single A to Z letter is lowered: in a shortcut it names the key, not the capital. The canonical form lists the modifier ids in send_keys.json order, then the key, joined by +."
	},
	"vectors": [
		{
			"id": "text_sentence",
			"kind": "text",
			"value": "bonjour cela va bien?",
			"canonical": "bonjour cela va bien?"
		},
